Open seat: Gavin Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's open governor's race pits Democrat Xavier Becerra against Republican Steve Hilton, and every major rating outfit calls it Solid or Safe Democratic. The state's D+12 partisan lean and an environment that has favored Democrats give Becerra a strong structural advantage in his bid to succeed Gavin Newsom.\n\nSeptember polls from Berkeley IGS, SurveyUSA, PPIC and the Berkeley Citrin Center all show Becerra ahead by 18 to 25 points among likely voters, and prediction markets price his chances around 96 percent. Hilton has slightly outraised Becerra and is campaigning on affordability, while headlines note lagging Democratic enthusiasm and soft views of Becerra himself. Those wrinkles suggest the final margin may land a bit below the polling average, but the race is not expected to be close.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}]}